  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 144 PM CDT Thu Jun 25 2026\n\nSaturday into early next week, the ridge will re-center over the \ndeep south of the CONUS as an upper level trough develops and \nspreads southward across much of the western U. S. While this will\ntheoretically bring shower and thunderstorm chances closer to our\nwestern counties, there will not be much discernible change in \nour forecast. Highs will continue to be warmer than normal for \nmost of the area, with highs ranging from the mid 90s in our \nsouthern counties, with upper 90s to around 100 degrees for the \nConcho Valley and Big Country areas. Winds will remain southerly \nthroughout the period, with speeds in the 10 to 20 mph range, \nalong with higher gusts during the day, and falling to around 10 \nmph during the overnight hours.",
